{
  "schema": "movegrow.motor-rules/0.1",
  "_note": "Descriptive, non-diagnostic rules compiled from clinical text (see sources.json). Every threshold carries its origin: 'literature' (taken from the cited description) or 'engineering_prior' (our starting value, to be calibrated). Severity: info < note < discuss < safety. 'safety' rules show safety-net guidance; they never state a diagnosis.",
  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "rhythm.fast_fine",
      "version": "0.1",
      "status": "enabled",
      "family": "rhythm",
      "analysis": "spectral",
      "band": "fast",
      "name": {
        "zh": "快速、细小的节律性抖动",
        "en": "Fast, fine rhythmic shaking"
      },
      "requires": {
        "min_fps": 24,
        "series": "raw",
        "context_exclude": [
          "held"
        ],
        "joints": [
          "leftShoulder",
          "rightShoulder",
          "leftHip",
          "rightHip"
        ],
        "min_coverage": 0.6
      },
      "params": {
        "f_lo": {
          "value": 6.0,
          "unit": "Hz",
          "origin": "literature",
          "source": "S01"
        },
        "f_hi": {
          "value": 12.0,
          "unit": "Hz",
          "origin": "engineering_prior",
          "note": "upper search bound; needs fs >= 24 Hz"
        },
        "min_prom_db": {
          "value": 8.0,
          "unit": "dB",
          "origin": "engineering_prior",
          "note": "spectral peak over local median (keypoint jitter is broadband)"
        },
        "min_rhythm": {
          "value": 0.4,
          "unit": "r",
          "origin": "engineering_prior"
        },
        "max_p2p_cm": {
          "value": 3.0,
          "unit": "cm",
          "origin": "literature",
          "source": "S01",
          "note": "converted from torso units with torso_cm prior"
        },
        "min_p2p_torso": {
          "value": 0.012,
          "unit": "torso",
          "origin": "engineering_prior",
          "note": "below this the peak is indistinguishable from keypoint jitter"
        },
        "max_rigid_r2": {
          "value": 0.6,
          "unit": "R2",
          "origin": "engineering_prior",
          "note": "reject windows where one similarity motion explains the shaking (camera shake)"
        }
      },
      "window_predicate": {
        "all": [
          {
            "f": "peak_hz",
            "op": "between",
            "v": [
              "$f_lo",
              "$f_hi"
            ]
          },
          {
            "f": "prominence_db",
            "op": ">=",
            "v": "$min_prom_db"
          },
          {
            "f": "rhythmicity",
            "op": ">=",
            "v": "$min_rhythm"
          },
          {
            "f": "amp_p2p_cm",
            "op": "<=",
            "v": "$max_p2p_cm"
          },
          {
            "f": "amp_p2p",
            "op": ">=",
            "v": "$min_p2p_torso"
          },
          {
            "f": "rigid_r2",
            "op": "<=",
            "v": "$max_rigid_r2"
          }
        ]
      },
      "episode": {
        "min_duration_s": 3.0,
        "merge_gap_s": 0.5,
        "freq_tol_hz": 1.0,
        "note": "engineering prior: >=3 overlapping 2-s windows with a stable peak frequency; isolated noise peaks wander in frequency"
      },
      "laterality": "any",
      "severity": "note",
      "message": {
        "zh": "{t0:.0f}–{t1:.0f} 秒：{limbs_zh}出现约 {hz:.1f} Hz 的细小节律性抖动，持续约 {dur:.1f} 秒（{laterality_zh}）。",
        "en": "{t0:.0f}–{t1:.0f} s: fine rhythmic shaking of the {limbs_en} at about {hz:.1f} Hz for {dur:.1f} s ({laterality_en})."
      },
      "explain": {
        "zh": "这与文献对新生儿细震颤 / jitteriness 的描述相符：频率高于 6 Hz、幅度小于约 3 cm，常见于健康新生儿，常两侧对称。区分它与抽搐的关键是：轻柔握住肢体时是否停止。",
        "en": "This matches published descriptions of newborn fine tremor or jitteriness: faster than 6 Hz and smaller than about 3 cm, common in healthy newborns and often on both sides. The key difference from a seizure is whether it stops when the limb is gently held."
      },
      "followup": {
        "zh": "下次出现时，请轻柔握住那只手或脚。停下来通常说明是良性抖动；如果握住也不停、伴随眼神凝视或面色/呼吸变化，请及时就医，并把这段视频给医生看。",
        "en": "Next time it happens, gently hold that hand or foot. If it stops, it is usually benign jitteriness. If it keeps going while held, or comes with staring or a change in colour or breathing, seek medical care and show this video."
      },
      "sources": [
        "S01",
        "S02",
        "S04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "rhythm.coarse",
      "version": "0.1",
      "status": "enabled",
      "family": "rhythm",
      "analysis": "spectral",
      "band": "fast",
      "name": {
        "zh": "较粗大的节律性抖动",
        "en": "Coarse rhythmic shaking"
      },
      "requires": {
        "min_fps": 24,
        "series": "raw",
        "context_exclude": [
          "held"
        ],
        "joints": [
          "leftShoulder",
          "rightShoulder",
          "leftHip",
          "rightHip"
        ],
        "min_coverage": 0.6
      },
      "params": {
        "f_lo": {
          "value": 4.5,
          "unit": "Hz",
          "origin": "engineering_prior",
          "note": "fast-band filter starts at 4 Hz; slower rhythms go to rhythm.slow_*"
        },
        "f_hi": {
          "value": 12.0,
          "unit": "Hz",
          "origin": "engineering_prior"
        },
        "coarse_f_below": {
          "value": 6.0,
          "unit": "Hz",
          "origin": "literature",
          "source": "S01"
        },
        "coarse_p2p_cm": {
          "value": 3.0,
          "unit": "cm",
          "origin": "literature",
          "source": "S01"
        },
        "min_prom_db": {
          "value": 8.0,
          "unit": "dB",
          "origin": "engineering_prior"
        },
        "min_rhythm": {
          "value": 0.4,
          "unit": "r",
          "origin": "engineering_prior"
        },
        "max_rigid_r2": {
          "value": 0.6,
          "unit": "R2",
          "origin": "engineering_prior"
        },
        "min_p2p_torso": {
          "value": 0.012,
          "unit": "torso",
          "origin": "engineering_prior"
        }
      },
      "window_predicate": {
        "all": [
          {
            "f": "peak_hz",
            "op": "between",
            "v": [
              "$f_lo",
              "$f_hi"
            ]
          },
          {
            "f": "prominence_db",
            "op": ">=",
            "v": "$min_prom_db"
          },
          {
            "f": "rhythmicity",
            "op": ">=",
            "v": "$min_rhythm"
          },
          {
            "f": "rigid_r2",
            "op": "<=",
            "v": "$max_rigid_r2"
          },
          {
            "f": "amp_p2p",
            "op": ">=",
            "v": "$min_p2p_torso"
          },
          {
            "any": [
              {
                "f": "peak_hz",
                "op": "<",
                "v": "$coarse_f_below"
              },
              {
                "f": "amp_p2p_cm",
                "op": ">",
                "v": "$coarse_p2p_cm"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "episode": {
        "min_duration_s": 3.0,
        "merge_gap_s": 0.5,
        "freq_tol_hz": 1.0,
        "note": "engineering prior: >=3 overlapping 2-s windows with a stable peak frequency; isolated noise peaks wander in frequency"
      },
      "laterality": "any",
      "severity": "discuss",
      "message": {
        "zh": "{t0:.0f}–{t1:.0f} 秒：{limbs_zh}出现约 {hz:.1f} Hz、幅度约 {p2p_cm:.1f} cm 的较粗大节律性抖动，持续约 {dur:.1f} 秒。",
        "en": "{t0:.0f}–{t1:.0f} s: coarse rhythmic shaking of the {limbs_en} at about {hz:.1f} Hz, ~{p2p_cm:.1f} cm, for {dur:.1f} s."
      },
      "explain": {
        "zh": "文献把频率较低、幅度较大的震颤称为粗震颤；与细震颤相比，它和安抚后仍不缓解的抖动一样，更值得让医生看看。幅度换算成厘米依赖身长先验，只是粗略估计。",
        "en": "Lower-frequency, larger-amplitude shaking is described as coarse tremor. Like shaking that does not settle with soothing, it is worth showing to a doctor. The size in centimetres relies on a body-size assumption and is only approximate."
      },
      "followup": {
        "zh": "请试着轻柔握住肢体或安抚宝宝，看是否停止；把这段视频带给儿科医生。若握住也不停或伴随凝视、面色/呼吸变化，请及时就医。",
        "en": "Try gently holding the limb or soothing your baby to see whether it stops, and bring this video to your paediatrician. If it continues while held, or comes with staring or a change in colour or breathing, seek medical care."
      },
      "sources": [
        "S01",
        "S04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "rhythm.slow_bout",
      "version": "0.1",
      "status": "enabled",
      "family": "rhythm",
      "analysis": "spectral",
      "band": "slow",
      "aggregate": true,
      "name": {
        "zh": "节律性踢腿 / 挥手",
        "en": "Rhythmic kicking / waving bouts"
      },
      "requires": {
        "min_fps": 24,
        "series": "raw",
        "context_exclude": [
          "held"
        ],
        "joints": [
          "leftShoulder",
          "rightShoulder",
          "leftHip",
          "rightHip"
        ],
        "min_coverage": 0.6
      },
      "params": {
        "f_lo": {
          "value": 0.75,
          "unit": "Hz",
          "origin": "engineering_prior"
        },
        "f_hi": {
          "value": 4.5,
          "unit": "Hz",
          "origin": "engineering_prior"
        },
        "min_prom_db": {
          "value": 6.0,
          "unit": "dB",
          "origin": "engineering_prior"
        },
        "min_rhythm": {
          "value": 0.35,
          "unit": "r",
          "origin": "engineering_prior"
        },
        "min_p2p_torso": {
          "value": 0.15,
          "unit": "torso",
          "origin": "engineering_prior"
        },
        "max_rigid_r2": {
          "value": 0.6,
          "unit": "R2",
          "origin": "engineering_prior"
        }
      },
      "window_predicate": {
        "all": [
          {
            "f": "peak_hz",
            "op": "between",
            "v": [
              "$f_lo",
              "$f_hi"
            ]
          },
          {
            "f": "prominence_db",
            "op": ">=",
            "v": "$min_prom_db"
          },
          {
            "f": "rhythmicity",
            "op": ">=",
            "v": "$min_rhythm"
          },
          {
            "f": "amp_p2p",
            "op": ">=",
            "v": "$min_p2p_torso"
          },
          {
            "f": "rigid_r2",
            "op": "<=",
            "v": "$max_rigid_r2"
          }
        ]
      },
      "episode": {
        "min_duration_s": 4.0,
        "merge_gap_s": 1.0,
        "note": "4 s window at >=0.75 Hz covers >=3 cycles (Thelen's 'at least three times')",
        "freq_tol_hz": 0.5
      },
      "laterality": "any",
      "severity": "info",
      "message": {
        "zh": "本次有 {n} 段节律性动作（共约 {total_s:.0f} 秒，典型频率 {hz:.1f} Hz），主要在{limbs_zh}。",
        "en": "{n} rhythmic bouts ({total_s:.0f} s total, typical {hz:.1f} Hz), mostly {limbs_en}."
      },
      "explain": {
        "zh": "有节律的踢腿、挥手、摇晃是婴儿正常运动发展的一部分，不同动作在不同月龄最常见。这里只是记录，便于看长期变化。",
        "en": "Rhythmic kicking, waving and rocking are a normal part of infant motor development, and different rhythms peak at different ages. This is recorded so you can see changes over time."
      },
      "sources": [
        "S10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "rhythm.slow_unilateral_sustained",
      "version": "0.1",
      "status": "enabled",
      "family": "rhythm",
      "analysis": "spectral",
      "band": "slow",
      "name": {
        "zh": "一侧肢体持续的规律抽动",
        "en": "Sustained one-sided rhythmic jerking"
      },
      "requires": {
        "min_fps": 24,
        "series": "raw",
        "context_exclude": [
          "held"
        ],
        "joints": [
          "leftShoulder",
          "rightShoulder",
          "leftHip",
          "rightHip"
        ],
        "min_coverage": 0.6
      },
      "params": {
        "f_lo": {
          "value": 1.0,
          "unit": "Hz",
          "origin": "literature",
          "source": "S02"
        },
        "f_hi": {
          "value": 4.0,
          "unit": "Hz",
          "origin": "literature",
          "source": "S02"
        },
        "min_prom_db": {
          "value": 8.0,
          "unit": "dB",
          "origin": "engineering_prior"
        },
        "min_rhythm": {
          "value": 0.5,
          "unit": "r",
          "origin": "engineering_prior"
        },
        "min_p2p_torso": {
          "value": 0.08,
          "unit": "torso",
          "origin": "engineering_prior"
        },
        "max_contra_ratio": {
          "value": 0.25,
          "unit": "power ratio",
          "origin": "engineering_prior",
          "note": "homologous limb power at the same frequency; 'one limb or one side' (S02)"
        },
        "max_rigid_r2": {
          "value": 0.6,
          "unit": "R2",
          "origin": "engineering_prior"
        }
      },
      "window_predicate": {
        "all": [
          {
            "f": "peak_hz",
            "op": "between",
            "v": [
              "$f_lo",
              "$f_hi"
            ]
          },
          {
            "f": "prominence_db",
            "op": ">=",
            "v": "$min_prom_db"
          },
          {
            "f": "rhythmicity",
            "op": ">=",
            "v": "$min_rhythm"
          },
          {
            "f": "amp_p2p",
            "op": ">=",
            "v": "$min_p2p_torso"
          },
          {
            "f": "contra_ratio",
            "op": "<=",
            "v": "$max_contra_ratio"
          },
          {
            "f": "rigid_r2",
            "op": "<=",
            "v": "$max_rigid_r2"
          }
        ]
      },
      "episode": {
        "min_duration_s": 10.0,
        "merge_gap_s": 1.0,
        "note": "engineering prior; normal rhythmic bouts are usually shorter and involve both sides",
        "freq_tol_hz": 0.5
      },
      "laterality": "unilateral",
      "severity": "safety",
      "message": {
        "zh": "{t0:.0f}–{t1:.0f} 秒：{limbs_zh}出现约 {hz:.1f} Hz 的规律性抽动，持续约 {dur:.0f} 秒，而另一侧相对安静。",
        "en": "{t0:.0f}–{t1:.0f} s: regular jerking of the {limbs_en} at about {hz:.1f} Hz for {dur:.0f} s while the other side stayed relatively quiet."
      },
      "explain": {
        "zh": "临床指南把“一侧肢体以每秒 1–4 次规律抽动、握住也不停”描述为需要和抽搐区分的情况；正常的节律性踢腿通常两侧都参与、也会被安抚或握住打断。App 无法判断这是不是抽搐。",
        "en": "Clinical guidance describes one limb or one side jerking regularly 1–4 times per second, not stopping when held, as something to tell apart from a seizure. Normal rhythmic kicking usually involves both sides and can be interrupted by soothing or holding. The app cannot tell whether this was a seizure."
      },
      "followup": {
        "zh": "如果再次出现：轻柔握住并换个姿势，看是否停止；记下持续时间并录像。若握住也不停、伴随凝视或面色/呼吸改变，请立即就医；持续 5 分钟以上请呼叫急救。",
        "en": "If it happens again: gently hold and reposition the limb to see if it stops, note how long it lasts and record it. If it continues while held, or comes with staring or a change in colour or breathing, seek medical care now; if it lasts 5 minutes or more, call emergency services."
      },
      "sources": [
        "S02",
        "S03",
        "S04",
        "S10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "burst.spasm_like_cluster",
      "version": "0.1",
      "status": "research",
      "family": "burst",
      "analysis": "burst",
      "name": {
        "zh": "成串出现的短暂同步动作",
        "en": "Clusters of brief synchronous movements"
      },
      "requires": {
        "min_fps": 15,
        "series": "smoothed",
        "context_exclude": [
          "held"
        ],
        "joints": [
          "leftShoulder",
          "rightShoulder",
          "leftHip",
          "rightHip"
        ],
        "min_coverage": 0.6
      },
      "params": {
        "abs_speed": {
          "value": 0.8,
          "unit": "torso/s",
          "origin": "engineering_prior"
        },
        "rel_speed": {
          "value": 4.0,
          "unit": "x session median",
          "origin": "engineering_prior"
        },
        "sync_tol_s": {
          "value": 0.15,
          "unit": "s",
          "origin": "engineering_prior",
          "note": "'synchronous' (S06)"
        },
        "min_limbs": {
          "value": 3,
          "unit": "limbs",
          "origin": "engineering_prior",
          "note": "'bilateral' (S06)"
        },
        "min_dur_s": {
          "value": 0.25,
          "unit": "s",
          "origin": "engineering_prior"
        },
        "max_dur_s": {
          "value": 3.0,
          "unit": "s",
          "origin": "literature",
          "source": "S05",
          "note": "S05: generally 1-3 s; S06: up to ~5 s"
        },
        "pre_quiet_ratio": {
          "value": 0.35,
          "unit": "ratio",
          "origin": "engineering_prior",
          "note": "'sudden': preceding 0.5-2 s much quieter than the event"
        },
        "min_interval_s": {
          "value": 2.0,
          "unit": "s",
          "origin": "engineering_prior"
        },
        "max_interval_s": {
          "value": 60.0,
          "unit": "s",
          "origin": "literature",
          "source": "S06"
        },
        "min_cluster": {
          "value": 3,
          "unit": "events",
          "origin": "engineering_prior"
        },
        "require_pair": {
          "value": true,
          "unit": "bool",
          "origin": "literature",
          "source": "S06",
          "note": "'bilateral': both arms or both legs take part"
        },
        "max_median_interval_s": {
          "value": 20.0,
          "unit": "s",
          "origin": "engineering_prior",
          "note": "S05 describes repeats every 5-10 s; 20 s leaves margin"
        },
        "max_surrogate_p": {
          "value": 0.05,
          "unit": "p",
          "origin": "engineering_prior",
          "note": "cluster must be larger than chance coincidences of the same baby's ordinary limb movements (limb-wise circular-shift surrogates)"
        },
        "require_axial": {
          "value": true,
          "unit": "bool",
          "origin": "literature",
          "source": "S06",
          "note": "axial involvement: S06 'axial muscle groups', S07 'drop head / bend forward'"
        },
        "min_axial": {
          "value": 0.05,
          "unit": "torso",
          "origin": "engineering_prior",
          "note": "change of head-to-shoulder distance or projected torso length vs the preceding 1.5 s"
        }
      },
      "session_predicate": {
        "all": [
          {
            "f": "largest_cluster",
            "op": ">=",
            "v": "$min_cluster"
          },
          {
            "f": "cluster_median_interval_s",
            "op": "<=",
            "v": "$max_median_interval_s"
          },
          {
            "f": "surrogate_p",
            "op": "<=",
            "v": "$max_surrogate_p"
          }
        ]
      },
      "age_weeks": {
        "min": 4,
        "max": 104,
        "source": "S05"
      },
      "severity": "safety",
      "message": {
        "zh": "检测到 {n} 次成串出现的短暂、四肢几乎同时的突然动作（每次约 {dur:.1f} 秒，间隔约 {iv:.0f} 秒）。",
        "en": "{n} brief, sudden, near-synchronous movements occurred in a cluster (~{dur:.1f} s each, ~{iv:.0f} s apart)."
      },
      "explain": {
        "zh": "医学资料把婴儿痉挛描述为成串出现、每次约 1–3 秒的突然屈曲或伸展，间隔通常不到 1 分钟，常在入睡或醒来时出现；它需要尽快由医生评估，家长拍的视频对诊断很有帮助。单次的惊跳不会触发这条规则（至少需要 3 次成串）。App 无法做出诊断。",
        "en": "Medical sources describe infantile spasms as clusters of sudden bends or stiffenings lasting about 1–3 seconds each, usually less than a minute apart, often when falling asleep or waking. They need prompt assessment by a doctor, and parent videos help. A single startle does not trigger this check (it needs at least 3 in a cluster). The app cannot make a diagnosis."
      },
      "followup": {
        "zh": "如果这与你在现场看到的相符，请尽快联系儿科医生并出示这段视频（App 可以导出带时间点的片段）。",
        "en": "If this matches what you saw, contact your paediatrician soon and show them this video (you can export the clip with its time stamps)."
      },
      "sources": [
        "S05",
        "S06",
        "S07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "posture.head_preference",
      "version": "0.1",
      "status": "enabled",
      "family": "posture",
      "analysis": "posture_side",
      "name": {
        "zh": "头部总是转向同一侧",
        "en": "Head-turn side preference"
      },
      "requires": {
        "min_fps": 5,
        "series": "smoothed",
