        "f": "head_yaw_sin",
        "thr": "$turn_thr"
      },
      "session_predicate": {
        "all": [
          {
            "f": "observed_s",
            "op": ">=",
            "v": "$min_observed_s"
          },
          {
            "f": "turned_frac",
            "op": ">=",
            "v": "$min_turned_frac"
          },
          {
            "f": "pref_index",
            "op": "abs>=",
            "v": "$min_abs_pi"
          }
        ]
      },
      "longitudinal": {
        "min_sessions": 3,
        "min_span_days": 7,
        "same_direction": true,
        "severity": "discuss"
      },
      "severity": "note",
      "message": {
        "zh": "本次转头时有 {pct:.0f}% 的时间朝向宝宝的{side_zh}（偏好指数 {pi:+.2f}，有效观察 {obs:.0f} 秒）。",
        "en": "When the head was turned, {pct:.0f}% of the time it faced the baby's {side_en} (preference index {pi:+.2f}, {obs:.0f} s observed)."
      },
      "explain": {
        "zh": "斜颈和体位性偏头的描述里，常见头一直偏向一侧、转向另一侧较少。单次录像容易受玩具或家长位置影响，所以只有多次、跨天都偏向同一侧才会提示与医生讨论。",
        "en": "Descriptions of torticollis and positional preference include a head that keeps turning to one side and turns less to the other. A single recording is easily influenced by where toys or people are, so only a preference seen across several days suggests talking to a clinician."
      },
      "followup": {
        "zh": "下次录像时把玩具或你自己放在宝宝较少看的那一侧，看看宝宝能否主动转过去；如果多次都偏向同一侧，可以和儿科医生或物理治疗师聊聊。",
        "en": "Next time, place a toy or yourself on the side your baby looks at less and see whether they turn that way. If several recordings show the same side, consider mentioning it to your paediatrician or a physiotherapist."
      },
      "sources": [
        "S12"
      ]
    },
