      "severity": "note",
      "message": {
        "zh": "转头时有 {pct:.0f}% 的时间呈击剑样姿势（脸朝向一侧手臂伸直、另一侧手臂屈曲），共 {n} 段。",
        "en": "ATNR-like fencing posture during {pct:.0f}% of head-turned time ({n} episodes)."
      },
      "message_expected": {
        "zh": "看到击剑样（ATNR 样）姿势。它在 1–4 个月最明显，通常 3–9 个月消失，属于这个月龄的常见表现。",
        "en": "An ATNR-like (fencing) posture was seen. It is most visible at 1–4 months and usually disappears by 3–9 months, so it is common at this age."
      },
      "explain": {
        "zh": "ATNR 是一种原始反射：头转向一侧时，脸朝向的一侧手臂伸展、后脑一侧屈曲；通常在 3–9 个月消失。月龄更大时仍经常、持续地出现，是值得和医生说的情况。",
        "en": "The ATNR is a primitive reflex: when the head turns, the arm on the face side extends and the other arm bends. It usually disappears by 3–9 months. Seeing it often and for long periods at an older age is worth mentioning to a doctor."
      },
      "followup": {
        "zh": "多录几次不同时间的视频；如果宝宝 6 个月后仍经常保持这个姿势、或很难从这个姿势中自己动出来，请和医生聊聊。",
        "en": "Record a few more videos at different times. If after 6 months your baby still often holds this posture, or has trouble moving out of it, talk to your doctor."
      },
      "sources": [
        "S11"
      ]
    },
