        "en": "The baby's {side_en} arm moved much less than the other (asymmetry index {ai:+.2f})."
      },
      "explain": {
        "zh": "研究发现，后来发展为单侧脑瘫的婴儿，在自发动作和够物中常出现两侧不对称，约 15 周后更明显；12 个月前出现明显的单手偏好也被视为需要评估的信号。遮挡、侧卧、玩具只放一边都会造成假象。",
        "en": "Studies found that infants who later develop one-sided cerebral palsy often move one side less in spontaneous movements and reaching, more clearly after about 15 weeks; a strong hand preference before 12 months is also a sign to have checked. Occlusion, lying on one side or toys placed on one side can all create this pattern."
